Before next release
===================

@image outside of a paragraph in @flushright is not flushed right.

investigate t/info_tests.t empty_in_flushright_index_entry issue, the
errors are not expected, as the end of lines should be removed when
doing the first flushright formatting.  It could be for the same reason as
the issue above, the count context is only added for paragraphs, not
for a whole @flushright.

Some tests do not use Perl anymore, but SKIP is based on Perl.  For example
'Skipping tests that require compatible unicode collation', or /a missing...

Use PARA_CONF_VARIABLES_LIST to have the same order of conf set in
ParagraphXS.xs that in convert_to_plaintext.c?  Not sure that it is
relevant, as, although it is possible to have ParagraphXS loaded and not
the other C libraries (no functioning iconv) it is unlikely to be
used for debug.  In pure Perl it could be relevant, though to try
to have the same Paragraph debug output as much as possible.

Have a look at texi2pod.pl in GCC

Add "shadow targets" or nodes to sectioning commands without nodes <- DONE
(and change USE_NODES to have 3 possible meaning?)
[no] output units are split at sections, and lone nodes are associated to
   the section.  A book-like setup, currently corresponding to USE_NODES=0.
   Sections have a "shadow" target added.
[nodes] output units are split at nodes, and lone sections do not have an
   associated node added.  They have a "shadow" target added.  Currently
   corresponds to USE_NODES=1.
[add] output units are split at nodes, but lone sections have an associated
   node automatically added.  Same as the tree transformation
   insert_nodes_for_sectioning_commands.  No shadow targets added.

No "shadow targets" nor nodes added when a node is associated to
a @*heading*, we should keep a track of this, such that users relying on
@heading know that it is different for heading and keep this in a TODO.

Verify that it works as expected in Info.


Document LATEX_TAGGED_PDF, change variable name if needed in code
and tests.
To document LaTeX customization variable to get accessible PDF.  This adds
\DocumentMetadata{tagging=on,
 <value of the customization variable>
}
with default for the value being
 lang=<BCP47 document-language-from-texinfo>,
 pdfstandard=ua-2,

and replace
\usepackage{amsmath}
\usepackage{amsfonts}
by
\usepackage{unicode-math}

